mfreadwrite/reader: rely on the video processor's sample allocator (Proton 164af86d, CW-Bug-Id 20833).

What it fixes: a game that plays video through a Media Foundation source reader with a D3D11
device manager (Unity's WindowsVideoMedia, Unreal's WmfMedia) asks DXGI for a shared handle on
each decoded frame's texture. The reader in this tree allocates those textures itself, without
the shared flags the video processor's own allocator would set from MF_SA_D3D11_SHARED, so DXMT
(which implements sharing through D3DKMT since 0.72) answers a null handle and the frame never
reaches the game: The Last Flame's menu video logs "Got null handle from
IDXGIResource::GetSharedHandle" ~14 times a second and never shows (highball#99, measured
2026-09-19 on x64-crossover26.3-r10, DXMT 0.80). 3Shain's diagnosis on 3Shain/dxmt#135 (Blue
Archive cutscenes) names this patch as the fix. The two companion leak fixes from Proton
(7bb1b147, e21244f7) are already in CrossOver 26.3's reader.c.

Verification: pending the first engine built with it (target: The Last Flame Prologue, Steam
2517810, menu video visible under DXMT; then Blue Archive-class Unity titles).

Upstream status: Proton-only as of 2026-09; not in upstream Wine 11.0 or CrossOver 26.3.

